 First, I will analyze the problem by examining the waveform data to understand the circuit's behavior. The inputs a and b are both one-bit signals, and the output q changes based on their values over time. Looking at the waveform, q is 0 when a and b are both 0, and it becomes 1 only when both a and b are 1. This suggests that q is the logical AND of a and b. Let me verify this by checking the waveform: at time 45ns, when a=1 and b=1, q=1; at 55ns, when a=0 and b=0, q=0; and at 85ns, when a=1 and b=1, q=1. This pattern confirms that q = a & b. Since the circuit is combinational, I'll implement this using a continuous assignment in Verilog.

[BEGIN]
module TopModule(
  input a,
  input b,
  output q
);
  assign q = a & b;
